    {
      "id": "HSqc5H8eZJNjarL9VIP-z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 740.5740364775842,
      "y": 50.66332878700956,
      "width": 709.3511824996663,
      "height": 1550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1106172592,
      "version": 8176,
      "versionNonce": 245176880,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780732720256,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- User should be able to upload text data and receive a unique URL.\n- User should be able to specify an expiration time for the paste.\n- User should be able to provide a custom alias for the URL (optional).\n- System should automatically expire and delete data after a specific\ntimespan.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- Analytics (e.g., redirection counts).\n- Uploading non-text media (images/videos).\n- Editing pastes after creation.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 1M DAU.\n- Read to Write ratio: 100:1\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- High reliability: Uploaded data must not be lost.\n- Low latency: Real-time access to pastes.\n- High availability: Ensuring continuous access to pastes.\n- Security: Paste links must be unguessable and unpredictable.\n- Constraints: Max 10MB per paste, size limits imposed on custom URLs.\n\n------- Out of Scope --------\n- protection against bad content.\n- User account creation and management.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: ~1,200 reads/sec\n    > Write QPS: ~10 pastes/sec\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 3k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 1M writes × 100 KB = 100 GB/day\n    > Yearly storage = 100 GB × 365 = 36.5 TB\n    > Total storage (5-year plan) = 36.5 TB × 5 = 182.5 TB\n    > replication: ~260 TB (using a 70% capacity model buffer)\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 10 write QPS × 100 KB = 1 MB/s\n    > Egress = 1,200 read QPS × 100 KB = 120 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 100M daily read requests × 100 KB × 0.20 = 2 TB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Paste\n- PasteMetadata\n- URL\n\n\n6) API Design \n\nPOST/paste\n    Input: {textData, expirationTime, customAlias}\n    Output: 201 Created, {pasteUrl}\n\nGET/paste/:pasteId\n    Output: 200 OK, {textData, createdAt, expirationTime}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- User should be able to upload text data and receive a unique URL.\n- User should be able to specify an expiration time for the paste.\n- User should be able to provide a custom alias for the URL (optional).\n- System should automatically expire and delete data after a specific timespan.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- Analytics (e.g., redirection counts).\n- Uploading non-text media (images/videos).\n- Editing pastes after creation.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- 1M DAU.\n- Read to Write ratio: 100:1\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- High reliability: Uploaded data must not be lost.\n- Low latency: Real-time access to pastes.\n- High availability: Ensuring continuous access to pastes.\n- Security: Paste links must be unguessable and unpredictable.\n- Constraints: Max 10MB per paste, size limits imposed on custom URLs.\n\n------- Out of Scope --------\n- protection against bad content.\n- User account creation and management.\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: ~1,200 reads/sec\n    > Write QPS: ~10 pastes/sec\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 3k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 1M writes × 100 KB = 100 GB/day\n    > Yearly storage = 100 GB × 365 = 36.5 TB\n    > Total storage (5-year plan) = 36.5 TB × 5 = 182.5 TB\n    > replication: ~260 TB (using a 70% capacity model buffer)\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 10 write QPS × 100 KB = 1 MB/s\n    > Egress = 1,200 read QPS × 100 KB = 120 MB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 100M daily read requests × 100 KB × 0.20 = 2 TB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Paste\n- PasteMetadata\n- URL\n\n\n6) API Design \n\nPOST/paste\n    Input: {textData, expirationTime, customAlias}\n    Output: 201 Created, {pasteUrl}\n\nGET/paste/:pasteId\n    Output: 200 OK, {textData, createdAt, expirationTime}",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
