    {
      "id": "3NpR-EDjW1gkOQZVnkex2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1529.6393493556975,
      "y": 488.1720388550534,
      "width": 770.9084738017215,
      "height": 329.44499750619724,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1257817955,
      "version": 10679,
      "versionNonce": 312889904,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780733162492,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Data Persistance:  \n    - bad solution: store everything in DB \n    - Good solution: use s3 for storing raw data and a db for metadata\n2) Unique Id generation: \n    - bad solution: Auto increment + base 62 encoding. The issue is\npredictability \n    - Good solution: Random 8 character string generation. 64^8 =281.5T\ncombinations. 1M*365*5 =1.8B needed for 5 years. Chances of collision low.\nWe use bloom filter for collision check.\n    - Good solution: Worker generates Unique random Ids and store in a pool.\nduring write the new id is grabbed from this pool. this is a bit complex\nsolution tho. \n3) EOD Cron job deletes expired content ",
      "fontSize": 20.273538308073675,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Data Persistance:  \n    - bad solution: store everything in DB \n    - Good solution: use s3 for storing raw data and a db for metadata\n2) Unique Id generation: \n    - bad solution: Auto increment + base 62 encoding. The issue is predictability \n    - Good solution: Random 8 character string generation. 64^8 =281.5T combinations. 1M*365*5 =1.8B needed for 5 years. Chances of collision low. We use bloom filter for collision check.\n    - Good solution: Worker generates Unique random Ids and store in a pool. during write the new id is grabbed from this pool. this is a bit complex solution tho. \n3) EOD Cron job deletes expired content ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
